<title>JAPAN: Key 182nd JGB yield falls to record low of 2.230%.</title>
<headline>Key 182nd JGB yield falls to record low of 2.230%.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-03-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>The yield of the benchmark 182nd 10-year Japanese government bond (JGB) fell to a record low of 2.230 percent in mid-afternoon trade on Friday.</p>
<p>A round of investor buying in cash JGBs, mainly the seven- to eight-year issues, helped push down the key bond yield, traders said.</p>
<p>-- Tokyo Treasury Desk +81-3-3432-8676</p>
</text>
